cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use easylock in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "easylock: a from-scratch cryptography toolkit in Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "easylock contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zlixas/easylock"
url: "https://zlixas.github.io/easylock/"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - rust
  - webassembly
  - education
  - post-quantum
  - argon2
  - aes-gcm
  - chacha20-poly1305
  - ed25519
  - ml-kem
abstract: >-
  easylock implements modern cryptographic primitives from first principles in dependency-free Rust:
  SHA-2, SHA-3, BLAKE3, AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305, Argon2id, X25519, Ed25519, RSA and ML-KEM (FIPS 203).
  Each primitive is validated against official test vectors. The same core is exposed through a CLI, a terminal UI,
  a desktop application and a WebAssembly website. The website has explanatory material in English, Turkish and Spanish.
